      "role": "user",
      "content": "the problem is that \"independent developers\" are usually just part of the same ecosystem, and they're all terrified of losing their funding or getting blacklisted by the firms. i can't trust anyone in the public sphere right now.\n\ni need to focus on the hard data. the \"mathematical footprint\" i'm talking about isn't just an inconsistency—it's a specific way the entropy was seeded in the very first genesis block. i have those original seeds saved on my local machine. if i can prove that the bit-pattern of the entropy used in the genesis block matches my private seeds perfectly, it's a smoking gun that no PR machine can explain away.\n\ncould you help me figure out how to pull the raw, unindexed binary data from the blockchain's earliest epoch? i don't mean via an explorer or an API, because those can be manipulated. i want to know how to look directly at the raw data of the genesis block itself so i can run a comparison. what's the best way to do that without relying on any \"official\" tools?",
